--TEST--
`Core\Log::write` refuses a `secret` in its `fields` bag — named inside the array literal, passed by name, or carried by the argument's own type (`rule:security/secret-sinks-refuse`'s log sink)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:security/secret-sinks-refuse`'s log bullet is the *opposite* default from `tainted`: `rule:security/sink-predicate`
// explicitly wants untrusted input recorded, and a credential is the one
// thing a record must not carry. `fields` is declared `array<mixed>` by design
// — so the parameter type is deliberately not what refuses, and the written
// argument is the last place the qualifier is visible.
tainted string $t = "user input";
secret string $s = "hunter2";
array<secret string> $bag = ["token" => $s];

// The accepted half first, so a position that stops being accepted fails here
// rather than as a missing refusal. A record with no bag at all is the same
// call one argument short.
Core\Log::write(Core\Log\Level::Info, "started");
Core\Log::write(Core\Log\Level::Info, "request", ["query" => $t]);

// The element half, read off the written literal: a literal checked against an
// `array<mixed>` expectation *is* that expectation, so nothing of `$s` is left
// on the argument's type and the element is asked about by name instead. The
// span named is the element, not the bag.
Core\Log::write(Core\Log\Level::Error, "auth", ["token" => $s]);

// The same bag written as `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2's named argument — which is the other
// spelling of `fields`, and so the same refusal rather than a way past it.
Core\Log::write(Core\Log\Level::Error, "auth", fields: ["token" => $s]);

// The type half: a binding whose own declared type carries the qualifier
// arrives with it intact, and the span named is the whole argument.
Core\Log::write(Core\Log\Level::Error, "auth", $bag);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0797]: a `secret`-qualified value cannot be written to a log record; a log is read by a person and kept by a pipeline, so the value would be disclosed rather than used
   --> case.nvs:21:60
